  narrationVoiceId: nPczCjzI2devNBz1zQrb
  introNarrationText: Opportunity was built to study Martian rocks and soils for
    clues that water once flowed there.
  solarPanelNarrationText: The solar arrays collected sunlight and converted it into
    electricity for the rover's batteries.
  cameraMastNarrationText: The camera mast raised stereo cameras for navigation and
    panoramic views of the terrain.
  instrumentArmNarrationText: The instrument arm placed science tools against rocks
    so Opportunity could examine their texture and chemistry.
  systemsCheckNarrationText: Power, vision, and science tools are accounted for.
    Opportunity is ready for launch.
